{"id": "MX-A-0009", "tier": "A", "stream": "Mathesis", "statement": "UC4 (physics). For circular orbits under an inverse-square central force, omega^2 * r^3 equals the gravitational parameter, and is therefore equal across any two orbits about the same primary. This is Kepler's third law with the reduced period tau = T/2pi, which removes pi from the statement and makes it exactly rational. The force law is a hypothesis parameter, never an axiom; the theorem is conditional on it.", "evidence_kind": "lean_axioms", "artifact": "lean/Mathesis/Applications/Kepler.lean#omega_sq_r_cubed,kepler_third", "supports": [], "audited_by": null, "supersedes": null}
